  "definition": "Permitted Quantities of Cannabis at an ATC",
  "effectiveDate": "2023-06-26",
  "historyNote": "#10731, eff 11-25-14; ss by #12653, eff 11-1-18; ss by #13673-A, eff 6-26-23",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "He-C 402.12",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-c400.html",
  "prefLabel": "He-C 402.12 Permitted Quantities of Cannabis at an ATC",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-C 402.12 Permitted Quantities of Cannabis at an ATC.\n\n(a) An ATC shall not possess or cultivate cannabis in excess of the following quantities:\n\n(1) Three mature cannabis plants, 12 seedlings, and 6 ounces of usable cannabis for each qualifying patient registered with the department; and\n\n(2) Up to an additional 80 mature cannabis plants, 160 seedlings, and 80 ounces of usable cannabis, including for start-up operations, to assist with a failed batch of cannabis, to allow sufficient quantity of cannabis for new qualifying patients, or to fill requests for the sale of cannabis to other ATCs.\n\n(b) The quantities in (a) above shall be inclusive of all cannabis or CIP possessed or being cultivated at all registered premises under the control of the ATC.\n\nSource. #10731, eff 11-25-14; ss by #12653, eff 11-1-18; ss by #13673-A, eff 6-26-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-c400.html"
